# Deny by default.
#
# Everything under data/ is runtime state, never source: the SQLite database
# and its WAL/SHM sidecars, the isolated e2e database, session logs and
# artifacts, uploads, applied migrations, dated pre-operation snapshots, and
# `mcp-user-global.json` (the ownership manifest for
# lib/mcp/user-global-sync.ts — it records which third-party MCP servers Arij
# last wrote into omp's mcp.json and agy's register on THIS box).
#
# This file used to enumerate those artifacts one by one, which meant every
# new runtime directory leaked into `git status` until a human noticed.
# `backups/` did exactly that: 472 MB of SQLite board snapshot and comment
# archive sat untracked, one `git add -A` away from a half-gigabyte commit of
# ticket, session, and prompt content. Enumeration fails open; a denylist
# fails closed, so the next artifact directory is ignored the day it appears.
#
# If something under data/ ever has to be tracked, un-ignore it explicitly
# below. Note that git does not descend into an ignored directory, so a nested
# path needs each parent un-ignored first (`!sub/`, then `!sub/file`).
#
# Tailwind is unaffected either way: app/globals.css pins the scan with
# `@import "tailwindcss" source(none)` plus explicit `@source` entries for
# app/, components/, hooks/ and lib/, so data/ is never scanned for utility
# candidates regardless of its ignore state.
*
!.gitignore
